WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.166 --> 00:00:01.134
Hey Crazies.

00:00:01.134 --> 00:00:04.404
I want to start by letting you know that I am not quitting YouTube.

00:00:04.504 --> 00:00:08.742
I know there's been a whole string of those videos, the best of which from Tom Scott.

00:00:08.942 --> 00:00:10.477
Godspeed, Tom.

00:00:10.477 --> 00:00:14.748
That being said, I do need to make a few changes for this to be sustainable.

00:00:14.848 --> 00:00:16.649
[Transition Screen Music]

00:00:16.916 --> 00:00:18.718
This first one is the big one.

00:00:18.718 --> 00:00:21.287
I want the channel to be viewer supported.

00:00:21.388 --> 00:00:26.760
Up until recently, Science Asylum revenue was mostly made up of three equal slices:

00:00:26.760 --> 00:00:31.464
Sponsors, which are branded segments that I read and embed into a video;

00:00:31.464 --> 00:00:36.302
YouTube ads that run before, after, or sometimes in the middle of a video;

00:00:36.302 --> 00:00:41.841
and Patreon, a platform that helps creators get financial support directly from viewers.

00:00:41.841 --> 00:00:44.644
Sponsors are a huge source of stress for me,

00:00:44.644 --> 00:00:47.080
not because of any specific brands I've worked with.

00:00:47.080 --> 00:00:49.115
I've always been pretty choosy about that.

00:00:49.115 --> 00:00:54.421
The number of sponsors I have turned away for moral or ethical reasons, it's a lot.

00:00:54.421 --> 00:01:00.093
But I think we can all agree that sponsored segments kind of pollute the viewing experience.

00:01:00.093 --> 00:01:02.896
It makes me miserable every time and I hate it.

00:01:02.896 --> 00:01:06.332
So I'm going to try not to take any sponsors in 2024,

00:01:06.332 --> 00:01:10.370
but that means a huge chunk of my revenue just disappears.

00:01:10.470 --> 00:01:15.475
To make up for the loss, I've started freelancing again, but getting your help would be better.

00:01:15.475 --> 00:01:18.378
If you have it to spare and feel like my work deserves it,

00:01:18.378 --> 00:01:21.581
please consider supporting the Science Asylum through Patreon.

00:01:21.581 --> 00:01:23.383
For as little as $1 per month,

00:01:23.383 --> 00:01:27.320
you get access to a live Q&amp;A we do at the end of every month.

00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:30.623
It's a pretty good time and we'd all love some new faces in the chat.

00:01:30.623 --> 00:01:33.660
You'll also get access to the Science Asylum Discord server,

00:01:33.660 --> 00:01:35.728
where deeper discussions can happen.

00:01:35.728 --> 00:01:37.464
Sustainability is key though,

00:01:37.464 --> 00:01:41.167
so please do not overextend yourself trying to support us.

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:45.205
If you'd prefer, YouTube memberships are a great alternative to Patreon.

00:01:45.205 --> 00:01:47.740
You'll still get access to the monthly live stream,

00:01:47.740 --> 00:01:51.644
an icon next your name in the comments, and some custom emojis.

00:01:51.644 --> 00:01:55.982
If a one time purchase is more your speed, I have an advanced physics book for sale.

00:01:55.982 --> 00:01:58.952
Speaking of which, the price is going up at the end of January.

00:01:58.952 --> 00:02:00.787
So if you were on the fence about buying it,

00:02:00.787 --> 00:02:02.889
now's your chance to get it at the lower price.

00:02:02.889 --> 00:02:05.258
Links to all of these options are in the doobly doo.

00:02:05.258 --> 00:02:10.363
And if financial support just isn't in the cards for you right now, I completely understand.

00:02:10.363 --> 00:02:13.466
Your continued viewership is greatly appreciated.

00:02:13.566 --> 00:02:15.368
[Transition Screen Music]

00:02:15.568 --> 00:02:20.940
For years, I've been failing to convince the normies to care about the topics I'm into

00:02:20.940 --> 00:02:24.244
and I'm not interested in covering most of the stuff that they're into.

00:02:24.244 --> 00:02:25.845
Let's face it, I'm weird.

00:02:25.845 --> 00:02:27.747
So I'm done looking at analytics.

00:02:27.747 --> 00:02:29.015
They shouldn't matter.

00:02:29.015 --> 00:02:31.818
I'm going to embrace who I am and make the videos

00:02:31.818 --> 00:02:35.622
I want to make regardless of whether or not they'll perform well.

00:02:35.622 --> 00:02:38.758
My video on Planetary Rings is a good example of this.

00:02:38.758 --> 00:02:43.496
I need to convince myself that below average performance does not equal bad.

00:02:43.496 --> 00:02:47.000
I loved making this video and I thought it turned out really good.

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:51.070
Anyway, it's become clear to me that I have no idea what makes a banger.

00:02:51.070 --> 00:02:53.606
And when they do happen, they're unpredictable.

00:02:53.606 --> 00:02:56.476
Something I learned the hard way back in 2022.

00:02:56.476 --> 00:03:01.681
I'm just so tired of worrying about whether or not my videos have a broad reach.

00:03:01.681 --> 00:03:04.484
You're the people I want to make videos for anyway.

00:03:04.484 --> 00:03:07.253
So again, if you can, please support my work.

00:03:07.353 --> 00:03:09.155
[Transition Screen Music]

00:03:09.455 --> 00:03:11.624
No more midroll YouTube ads.

00:03:11.624 --> 00:03:14.360
The ads that run before and after the video are fine.

00:03:14.360 --> 00:03:15.795
Those are going to stay for now.

00:03:15.795 --> 00:03:18.831
I'm just dropping the ones that run in the middle of the video.

00:03:18.831 --> 00:03:20.133
I've always felt sick about it,

00:03:20.133 --> 00:03:23.937
and YouTube keeps making them more awkward and intrusive over time.

00:03:23.937 --> 00:03:25.939
I'm done. They're going back off.

00:03:25.939 --> 00:03:28.708
Are these changes? I'm making terrible business decisions.

00:03:28.708 --> 00:03:31.077
Yes. I'm a terrible businessman.

00:03:31.077 --> 00:03:35.648
If I was a good one, I would have capitalized on the viral videos I had two years ago

00:03:35.648 --> 00:03:38.985
and hired a team to crank out content every single week.

00:03:38.985 --> 00:03:43.122
The quality, length, and schedule would be machine level consistent.

00:03:43.122 --> 00:03:45.258
I'd basically be Wendover Productions.

00:03:45.258 --> 00:03:48.027
Nothing against Sam. That's just not my journey.

00:03:48.027 --> 00:03:51.598
I don't want this to be a business. I don't want to be a manager.

00:03:51.598 --> 00:03:54.167
I'm an educator. I want to educate.

00:03:54.167 --> 00:03:57.036
All I want to do is teach you stuff that I think is interesting

00:03:57.036 --> 00:03:58.738
and be able to pay my bills.

00:03:58.738 --> 00:04:01.507
That's it. I have no bigger ambitions.

00:04:01.507 --> 00:04:05.578
So again, again, please consider supporting my work in 2024.

00:04:05.578 --> 00:04:09.649
And to those of you who already financially support me, thank you so much.

00:04:09.649 --> 00:04:11.851
You're the reason I haven't quit yet.

00:04:11.851 --> 00:04:14.220
Physics has always been a hard sell on YouTube,

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:16.089
and I'm kind of an acquired taste.

00:04:16.089 --> 00:04:17.323
Let's be weird together.

00:04:17.323 --> 00:04:21.127
And until next time, remember, it's okay to be a little crazy.

